(3411864, 474219, 27514, '<td valign="top">ooooooooo. I love love love love this image. what a great expression and what great photoshop work...<br/>tonality is just great. <br/>this is my pick for number one<br/> <br/>edit* I have come back to this image about 5 times now. I just love it''s impact.</td>', 'ooooooooo. I love love love love this image. what a great expression and what great photoshop work...tonality is just great. this is my pick for number one edit* I have come back to this image about 5 times now. I just love it''s impact.', '2007-02-28 00:58:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3411866, 475260, 62637, '<td valign="top">so small!  why?!  i hope you dont mind, but i looked at the exif for this one (i usually do when photos are abnormally small) and as i suspected, you didnt use save for web.  and why on earth is your dpi 300??  I see you used CS2:  next time, set your resolution to 640 pixels in one direction, then instead of "save as" go "save for web" and adjust the quality slider until the file size below your image is under 150kb.  feel free to PM me if youre not clear on that one, it really is a shame to see a photo hammered for such a silly reason as "its too small"</td>', 'so small!  why?!  i hope you dont mind, but i looked at the exif for this one (i usually do when photos are abnormally small) and as i suspected, you didnt use save for web.  and why on earth is your dpi 300??  I see you used CS2:  next time, set your resolution to 640 pixels in one direction, then instead of "save as" go "save for web" and adjust the quality slider until the file size below your image is under 150kb.  feel free to PM me if youre not clear on that one, it really is a shame to see a photo hammered for such a silly reason as "its too small"', '2007-02-28 00:58:23.000000', NULL, 1),
