(3437747, 476127, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by noraneko:</b></div><hr/><i> Cool idea, but the realization could use a little work - keys aren''t quite in focus, and bag texture is a bit distracting. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Interesting, as I figured part of the goal of this challenge was to shoot within a limited tonal range while still maintaining detail -- I deliberately chose the texture of the camera bag to show off that aspect.</td>', 'Originally posted by noraneko: Cool idea, but the realization could use a little work - keys aren''t quite in focus, and bag texture is a bit distracting.  Interesting, as I figured part of the goal of this challenge was to shoot within a limited tonal range while still maintaining detail -- I deliberately chose the texture of the camera bag to show off that aspect.', '2007-03-07 11:18:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(3437774, 476655, 45651, '<td valign="top">The image low key but the contrast is flat I would suggest bringing up the midtones and highlights but keep the shadows very dark. I would have scored this a 5 due to the contrast issue. <br/> <br/>I also entered a mannequin image it did OK but I was hoping for a finish above 6.  I have a feeling that real people score better than masks and Mannequins.</td>', 'The image low key but the contrast is flat I would suggest bringing up the midtones and highlights but keep the shadows very dark. I would have scored this a 5 due to the contrast issue.  I also entered a mannequin image it did OK but I was hoping for a finish above 6.  I have a feeling that real people score better than masks and Mannequins.', '2007-03-07 11:23:36.000000', NULL, 0),
