(3439287, 476822, 43073, '<td valign="top">As the others have said, I didn''t find the subject interesting enough, and scored it a bit low for that (4), as well as the distraction I felt in seeing the stereo controls right under the wheel (I might have cropped it a bit tighter; my monitor resolution means I need to move the page to see all of portrait images, and those controls jumped at me when I saw the image). Nicely lit, though, and definitely low-key to my untrained eyes.</td>', 'As the others have said, I didn''t find the subject interesting enough, and scored it a bit low for that (4), as well as the distraction I felt in seeing the stereo controls right under the wheel (I might have cropped it a bit tighter; my monitor resolution means I need to move the page to see all of portrait images, and those controls jumped at me when I saw the image). Nicely lit, though, and definitely low-key to my untrained eyes.', '2007-03-07 16:30:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439288, 476659, 13719, '<td valign="top">beautiful B&amp;W just awesome</td>', 'beautiful B&W just awesome', '2007-03-07 16:30:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439314, 474189, 43073, '<td valign="top">Came over from the thread; disappointing that no one else has offered comments here, but I''ll do my best. To start off, the simplest thing for me to say is that this didn''t look low-key to me. Instead, it seemed more like an evening sunset shot than a low-key shot. As an image, I quite like it, actually, as I think it''s well composed and nicely shot (though I''m not fond of subjects that are completely shadowed, it works well enough here as there are other interesting elements to the photo).</td>', 'Came over from the thread; disappointing that no one else has offered comments here, but I''ll do my best. To start off, the simplest thing for me to say is that this didn''t look low-key to me. Instead, it seemed more like an evening sunset shot than a low-key shot. As an image, I quite like it, actually, as I think it''s well composed and nicely shot (though I''m not fond of subjects that are completely shadowed, it works well enough here as there are other interesting elements to the photo).', '2007-03-07 16:34:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439347, 476655, 43073, '<td valign="top">Read your request for comments on the thread; this wasn''t an image I liked, but this is primarily because of the subject matter. It just didn''t interest me, and while it was lit well for and appropriate to the challenge, it didn''t do anything to overcome my initial reaction to the subject matter. On that, there is probably little you can do about this kind of reaction; pick a shot you like, and some other people won''t. Not a statement about the image quality, but about its appeal subjectively. If you want my vote, shoot puppy dogs and babies &lt;joke&gt;</td>', 'Read your request for comments on the thread; this wasn''t an image I liked, but this is primarily because of the subject matter. It just didn''t interest me, and while it was lit well for and appropriate to the challenge, it didn''t do anything to overcome my initial reaction to the subject matter. On that, there is probably little you can do about this kind of reaction; pick a shot you like, and some other people won''t. Not a statement about the image quality, but about its appeal subjectively. If you want my vote, shoot puppy dogs and babies <joke>', '2007-03-07 16:37:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439367, 474849, 43073, '<td valign="top">Deb, I''m here after reading the thread; I didn''t score this image highly, though I hope you know I usually like your shots. Setups to me need to be special, and the subject matter here just didn''t grab me. It was well lit, though more shadows might have helped the low-key feel jump at you (the "normally" lit table to the right distracted me a bit when I first saw the image), and the composition and execution were spot on. I''m just not big on thread . . .</td>', 'Deb, I''m here after reading the thread; I didn''t score this image highly, though I hope you know I usually like your shots. Setups to me need to be special, and the subject matter here just didn''t grab me. It was well lit, though more shadows might have helped the low-key feel jump at you (the "normally" lit table to the right distracted me a bit when I first saw the image), and the composition and execution were spot on. I''m just not big on thread . . .', '2007-03-07 16:40:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439369, 476613, 73575, '<td valign="top">I posted during the challenge, I thought...<br/>to recap, I love this shot! The stars, the glow of the moon, the compostition... I only wish the headlights(?) at left center weren''t there.</td>', 'I posted during the challenge, I thought...to recap, I love this shot! The stars, the glow of the moon, the compostition... I only wish the headlights(?) at left center weren''t there.', '2007-03-07 16:40:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439376, 474632, 43073, '<td valign="top">Can''t help you too much with why this scored where it did; I gave it a seven. Had everything I was looking for on the whole, and I thought it was a good shot. Sorry I''m not being more "critical" here.</td>', 'Can''t help you too much with why this scored where it did; I gave it a seven. Had everything I was looking for on the whole, and I thought it was a good shot. Sorry I''m not being more "critical" here.', '2007-03-07 16:42:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439475, 476219, 43073, '<td valign="top">My reaction to this shot was I think based primarily on the effect the colors had on the light in the image. They look bright, but really the whole thing seems bright. I''m not one to say that low key has to be B&amp;W, but the red really exaggerates (at least to my eyes) the overall brightness it. This to me seemed bright overall (even with the background darkened as it was) to be low key. I did a quick conversion to black and white; do that and take a look, it might help you see what I think I was seeing in the color version. The histogram might help, too; it shows a spike at the dark end and then pretty level across the rest of the spectrum. Not definitive, but says something. I hope that helps a bit, sorry for rambling on.</td>', 'My reaction to this shot was I think based primarily on the effect the colors had on the light in the image. They look bright, but really the whole thing seems bright. I''m not one to say that low key has to be B&W, but the red really exaggerates (at least to my eyes) the overall brightness it. This to me seemed bright overall (even with the background darkened as it was) to be low key. I did a quick conversion to black and white; do that and take a look, it might help you see what I think I was seeing in the color version. The histogram might help, too; it shows a spike at the dark end and then pretty level across the rest of the spectrum. Not definitive, but says something. I hope that helps a bit, sorry for rambling on.', '2007-03-07 16:54:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439498, 473207, 43073, '<td valign="top">I think this shot didn''t grab me because of the color in the lighting; I felt it distracted from the subject matter and the general feel of the shot as a low-key shot. I''m not saying it''s not low-key, and I''m not saying that it should have been black and white, but the highs got lost in the color for me, and that made it less appealing. Hope that helps you see what I saw.</td>', 'I think this shot didn''t grab me because of the color in the lighting; I felt it distracted from the subject matter and the general feel of the shot as a low-key shot. I''m not saying it''s not low-key, and I''m not saying that it should have been black and white, but the highs got lost in the color for me, and that made it less appealing. Hope that helps you see what I saw.', '2007-03-07 16:59:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439500, 475919, 30982, '<td valign="top">I think this works very well for low key - you brought out the texture and design on the flask very well.  My only nit would be that the separation of the base of the flask from the surface upon which it is sitting is hard to discern.</td>', 'I think this works very well for low key - you brought out the texture and design on the flask very well.  My only nit would be that the separation of the base of the flask from the surface upon which it is sitting is hard to discern.', '2007-03-07 16:59:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3439506, 476091, 30982, '<td valign="top">Nah, keep using pets.  They''re the only models I have, too, since I don''t use me.  I liked the softness of the fur in this, but would have liked to have seen more of the eyes.</td>', 'Nah, keep using pets.  They''re the only models I have, too, since I don''t use me.  I liked the softness of the fur in this, but would have liked to have seen more of the eyes.', '2007-03-07 17:00:37.000000', NULL, 0),
