(3475994, 476540, 3032, '<td valign="top">Amazing. 51st place, almost a 6, 260 views and only one comment...<br/>But I agree with Gerda. The rose now roughle divides the frame into halves and that doesn''t work well.<br/>A more diagonal framefilling approach might have created more depth and worked better. But who am I, you still kick my butt in any challenge. :)<br/> <br/></td>', 'Amazing. 51st place, almost a 6, 260 views and only one comment...But I agree with Gerda. The rose now roughle divides the frame into halves and that doesn''t work well.A more diagonal framefilling approach might have created more depth and worked better. But who am I, you still kick my butt in any challenge. :) ', '2007-03-20 18:16:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3484482, 476665, 54228, '<td valign="top">I think I''d prefer a little more negative space into the top right, to give a bit of a lonely feel. The reflection seems to fit though, it gives the sense that the flower is actually sitting somewhere. Perhaps you could include a little more of that ''somewhere'' (in VERY low key of course).</td>', 'I think I''d prefer a little more negative space into the top right, to give a bit of a lonely feel. The reflection seems to fit though, it gives the sense that the flower is actually sitting somewhere. Perhaps you could include a little more of that ''somewhere'' (in VERY low key of course).', '2007-03-23 22:37:06.000000', NULL, 0),
